   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The rule of earlier action with «nachdem»",
     "texto": [
      "**Nachdem** means \"after\". As the action of the «nachdem» clause always happened before the main clause action, the verb tenses must follow a strict sequence:",
      "1. If the main action is narrated in the past (Präteritum or Perfekt), the «nachdem» time clause must go in the **Plusquamperfekt**: **Nachdem sie den Vertrag unterschrieben hatte, feierte sie mit den Kollegen**.",
      "2. If the main action is in the present (Präsens) or future (Futur I), the «nachdem» time clause takes the **Perfekt**: **Nachdem du die E-Mail geschickt hast, machen wir Mittagspause**.",
      "Remember that «nachdem» is a subordinating conjunction: the conjugated verb goes at the absolute end of its clause."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Main clause",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Subordinate clause with «nachdem»",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
